    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d497-a2">

                <pb facs="0563" n="543" sameAs="frus:frus1864p3/pg543"/>

                <head ana="#head_untitled-missing-head-in-printed-volume">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Office
                                United States Military Telegraph</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">War
                                Department.</hi></placeName> [<date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content" calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1864-08-02">August 2, 1864</date>].</dateline></opener>
                <p>The following telegram received at Washington, October 15, 1864, 10.15 p. m.—from
                    San Francisco, October 14, 1864:</p>
                <p rendition="#right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">United States Legation</hi>, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Yedo, August</hi> 2, 1864.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Legation indemnity paid; written agreement
                    given for payment of Pembroke indemnity, principal and interest, within thirty
                    days, and for submission of all other claims to arbitration to Emperor of
                    Russia, if not in meantime arranged.</p>
                <p>Yours, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ROBERT H. PRUYN, <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Resident in
                            Japan.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, &amp;c., &amp;c.,
                        &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
